ort-validation.v1","summary":"The report says omarchy-menu-keybindings and --print hang forever when the user Hyprland Lua config iterates an hl list getter (hl.get_monitors(), hl.get_windows(), hl.get_workspaces()) with ipairs at config-evaluation time, while Hyprland itself stays fine. build_lua_bind_cache in bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings re-evaluates ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua under a stub hl whose catch-all __index answers every key with a truthy noop sentinel, so ipairs over a list getter never reaches nil and the lua subprocess spins forever; the bash while-read loop feeding off it blocks, and the menu neither opens nor refuses. The reproducer drives the real bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings --print with a stock user config tree plus the reported one line of user Lua, placed ahead of require(\"default.hypr.omarchy\") because at this baseline that require reaches default/hypr/qconsole.lua, whose numeric comparison throws against the same stub and makes the pcall abort the scan before later user files load (the masking the issue thread documents) - the defect is the stub's non-terminating ipairs, reached by any user Lua the scan evaluates. The engine run is killed by the reproducer's own watchdog after 8 seconds and prints the defect-present marker; with the list getters stubbed to real empty tables the same run terminates and lists the bindings. KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-SCAN-DOFILE-ABORT is the same stub aborting the scan early on a throwing comparison (later binds silently vanish) rather than never returning; KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-NO-TIMEOUT is unbounded waits in hyprctl binds / xkbcli compile-keymap, not the lua subprocess walking the hl stub.","validationDigest":"sha256:beee102499b700ee1d51d101e6b3cdc955ca407f1042b0c273d83ddc72704ce0","validationId":"rval-b4814042803ea66adfa443ac97401769","verdict":"confirmed"}
